  "document": "Mangareva Statue\nThe Mangareva Statue or \"Deity Figure from Mangareva\" is an important wooden sculpture of a male god that was made on the Pacific island of Mangareva in French Polynesia. The idol was given to English missionaries in the early nineteenth century as the local population converted to Christianity. It was eventually bought by the British Museum in 1911."
